statement:
Over any field $F$, at any level $\ell\ge1$, with $q_H
e1$ of finite order $e\ge2$ and split $Q_a=q_H^{c_a}$, use the actual multipartition-summand Schur cover and standards of [[thm-cyclotomic-schur-standards-and-schur-functor-control-block-linkage]] and the INTEGER $J_{\lambda\mu}$ of [[thm-cyclotomic-schur-jantzen-sum-formula-from-rim-hook-valuations]]. Let $\sim_J$ be the equivalence generated by $J_{\lambda\mu}
e0$ or $J_{\mu\lambda}
e0$. Then $\lambda\sim_J\mu$ iff $\Delta^\lambda,\Delta^\mu$ belong to one Schur block iff their Murphy Specht modules $S^\lambda,S^\mu$ belong to one Hecke block. Rank0 has the single empty class. No residue-content block assertion is an input.
